draw: GL point rasterization option for wide points

draw_wide_point_gl() makes the wide point stage emit GL-rounded point
sizes at snapped positions without the 1/8 pixel bias, and exact
squares for sprites.  Off by default; chrome9 enables it.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

diff -urNp a/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_context.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_context.c
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_context.c	2026-10-11 20:23:18.590294053 +0200
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/draw/draw_context.c	2026-10-11 20:23:18.591294064 +0200
@@ -508,6 +508,19 @@ draw_wide_point_threshold(struct draw_co
 
 
 /**
+ * Draw aliased points as GL does: the size rounded to an integer (at least
+ * one) and the square snapped to pixel edges; sprites as the exact square.
+ * Without this the quads keep the fractional size and a 1/8 pixel bias.
+ */
+void
+draw_wide_point_gl(struct draw_context *draw, bool gl)
+{
+   draw_do_flush(draw, DRAW_FLUSH_STATE_CHANGE);
+   draw->pipeline.wide_point_gl = gl;
+}
+
+
+/**
  * Should the draw module handle point->quad conversion for drawing sprites?
  */
 void
